  "method": "Viewed actual native/raw/master and actual decoded Mid/High, native+replacement identical BOX32/16 pairs, full literal X/Y contacts/corners and2x2repeats, decoded height/normalized XYZ, neutral grey180 and textured opposed lights. Reused source-measured witness locations only after current source-crop inspection; no author verdict substituted for these observations.",
  "observations": {
    "material": "One dense dry grey stone slab reads as tangible pitted mineral material rather than abstract grain. Irregular pores, worn/chipped patches and subdued grey/olive variation remain coherent at High512 and Mid256. Limestone-like material is plausible interpretation, not measured geology.",
    "formsColourAndScale": "The broad single slab, sparse larger dark pits/chips and restrained edge relationships remain representative at BOX32/16. Enhanced material is somewhat brighter/more detailed than Low; this does not alter the single-face structure or introduce extra joints/objects. Same-RGB layered repair leaves photographic forms and distance appearance intact.",
    "repeatsAndCorners": "Whole literal X and Y strips, four-corner junctions and repeated views at both tiers preserve the native narrow straight slab contacts. The bright/dark arris relationships belong to this source and remain restrained. No additional interior division, broad perimeter band or unexplained straight cut through a continuous face was found. This intentional-joint case is distinct from a continuous-stone/fibre field cut.",
    "physicalRelief": "Current neutral opposed lights read as a broad nearly flat face with shallow local roughness/pits and recessed existing contacts. The prior broad olive/right scalar depression is reduced and no longer reads as the slab architecture. Source A/C/D faces sit above F/G shallow-pit neighborhoods and the decoded joint centers at both tiers. Fine detail remains restrained, particularly Mid; much tiny pore contrast remains photographic RGB.",
    "semanticBoundaries": "B is a dark fleck/face mixture; E is a chipped/inclusion mixture. They are not pure-face or pure-pit acceptance samples. Mid L/T neighborhoods have only0.6mean joint-mask support and include face/transition pixels, with correspondingly broad height ranges; their center heights and actual lit contacts, not a claim of pure neighborhood depth, support the bounded joint interpretation. High mask purity proves raster support, not independent material purity or exact hidden geometry.",
    "coarseScalarEvidence": {
      "initialSlopeXY": [
        -0.10860647385126186,
        -0.02999422389750006
      ],
      "currentSlopeXY": [
        -0.005430323603845155,
        -0.0014997112845365201
      ],
      "interpretation": "About20x smaller color-correlated plane slope; quantitative implementation evidence complements actual neutral ART, not calibrated real-world depth."
    }
  },
